---
/* SUBMIT YOUR TRACK, reescrita 2026-08-16 (pase 12).

   Antes esta pagina vendia los 5 EUR como el lanzamiento a curadores externos,
   que es el servicio GRANDE: eso es playlist pitching y cuesta desde 100 EUR.
   Los 5 EUR son otra cosa, el envio a NUESTRAS listas. Dejarla como estaba
   dejaba dos paginas del mismo sitio prometiendo cosas distintas por el mismo
   dinero.

   NOTA PARA LAS GUARDAS DE LOS .BAT: no escribir aqui, ni en ningun comentario,
   la cadena literal que un .bat vaya a buscar con nocontains. Ya paso el 16/08
   y la comprobacion fallo contra mi propio comentario.

   EL PASO QUE FALLA, Y POR QUE ESTA EN NEGRITA. El cobro va por Ko-fi, y Ko-fi
   no tiene un campo obligatorio para el enlace: el artista lo pega en el mensaje
   del pago o no lo pega. Si no lo pega, hay 5 EUR y no hay cancion. Ese paso es
   el unico modo de fallo real del producto, asi que va numerado, en negrita y
   antes del boton, no en la letra pequena. */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { KOFI, PLAYLISTS_URL, PLAYLISTS, url } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="Submit your track"
  description="One Spotify link, 5 EUR, considered for the playlists 109MUSIC runs. Placement is not guaranteed and the playlists are public."
  activeSection="submit">
  <div class="slab">
   <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="kicker mono rise">109MUSIC · Playlists</p>
      <h1 class="display face rise">Submit your<br /><span class="lav">track</span></h1>
      <p class="statement rise">
        One Spotify link, <b>5 EUR</b>, considered for the two lists we actively
        programme. Placement is not guaranteed, and both lists are public, so you
        can check whether you fit before you pay.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta rise">
        <a class="btn" href={KOFI} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span>Submit on Ko-fi · 5 EUR</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="#the-playlists">
          <span>Hear the lists first</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
   </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section>
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">How it works</h2></div>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Pay the 5 EUR on Ko-fi, where we take submissions.</li>
        <li>
          <b>Paste the Spotify link to your track in the message box before you pay.</b>{' '}
          This is the one step that goes wrong. Without the link there is nothing for
          us to listen to, and we have no way of knowing who sent it.
        </li>
        <li>We listen. If it belongs on one of the lists, it goes on.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="keyfact">
        <span class="mono">The five euros buy a listen</span>
        <p>
          They do not buy a placement, and nobody who is honest will sell you one for
          five euros. What they buy is that a person hears the whole track and makes a
          real decision about it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="the-playlists">
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">The two lists</h2></div>
      <p class="sec-intro">
        Two lists, actively programmed, <b>22,000 saves between them</b>. They are
        public, so listen before you decide whether five euros is worth it.
      </p>

      {/* CARGA BAJO DEMANDA, y no es decoracion: el reproductor de Spotify hace
          36 peticiones a 7 dominios y planta seis cookies nada mas cargar, entre
          ellas un identificador publicitario y una cadena de consentimiento IAB.
          Dos de esos en una pagina, para quien solo esta leyendo, no se sostiene
          ni en peso ni en privacidad. Asi no se pide NADA a Spotify hasta que
          alguien pulsa play. El coste es un puñado de bytes de JS en linea. */}
      <div class="players">
        {PLAYLISTS.map((pl) => (
          <div class="player" data-embed={`https://open.spotify.com/embed/playlist/${pl.id}`}>
            <div class="player-face">
              <span class="player-name">{pl.name}</span>
              <span class="player-meta mono">{pl.saves} saves · {pl.line}</span>
              <button type="button" class="player-play" data-play>
                <span aria-hidden="true">▶</span> Play preview
              </button>
              <a class="player-out mono" href={pl.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open in Spotify →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="player-note mono">
        Nothing loads from Spotify until you press play.
      </p>

      <p class="sec-intro">
        If your record is nowhere near either of those, keep your five euros. We
        would rather tell you here than take it and send you a no.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">What you do not get</h2></div>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>A guaranteed placement. Anyone promising one is buying it.</li>
        <li>Bot streams, or playlists whose listeners are not real.</li>
        <li>
          Pitching to outside curators. That is the bigger service and it is priced
          differently: <a href={url('/services/#playlist-pitching')}>playlist pitching</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    /* Un solo listener delegado. Al pulsar, el bloque se sustituye por el iframe
       real. Antes de eso la pagina no ha hablado con Spotify ni una vez. */
    document.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
      var b = ev.target.closest && ev.target.closest('[data-play]');
      if (!b) return;
      var host = b.closest('.player');
      if (!host) return;
      var f = document.createElement('iframe');
      f.src = host.getAttribute('data-embed');
      f.width = '100%'; f.height = '352'; f.frameBorder = '0';
      f.loading = 'lazy'; f.title = 'Spotify player';
      f.allow = 'clipboard-write; encrypted-media; fullscreen; picture-in-picture';
      host.replaceChildren(f);
    });
  </script>
</Base>
